<article class="env-theorem" id="0GRR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GRR">Theorem <span data-tag="0GRR">106.16.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a Noetherian algebraic stack with affine diagonal. Let $B$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $F : \text{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}) \to \text{Mod}^{fg}_ B$ be a right exact tensor functor. Then $F$ comes from a unique morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \to \mathcal{X}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0GRJ" data-tag="0GRJ">106.16.1</a> we can extend $F$ uniquely to a right exact tensor functor $F : \mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}) \to \text{Mod}_ B$ commuting with all direct susms. Then we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0GRQ" data-tag="0GRQ">106.16.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>